%% Corrected from figures/mermaid/fig_3_5_sequence.mmd.
%% One normally completed heartbeat; failure boundary is stated explicitly below.
sequenceDiagram
  participant Agent as Agent
  participant Store as SQLite store
  participant Sources as Telemetry sources
  participant Model as Configured LLM
  participant Ntfy as ntfy
  Note over Agent,Sources: Prepare optional Docker log seed
  Agent->>Store: Read current-ruleset acknowledgements
  Store-->>Agent: Eligible known conditions
  Agent->>Sources: Collect configured telemetry
  Sources-->>Agent: Evidence and collection status
  Agent->>Model: Request bounded analysis
  Model-->>Agent: Response or provider error
  Note over Agent,Model: Validate response. Reported provider/parser failure becomes a high pipeline-failure verdict
  opt High or critical and Docker monitoring enabled
    Agent->>Sources: Collect extra Docker diagnostics
    Sources-->>Agent: Diagnostic result
  end
  opt High or critical
    Agent->>Ntfy: Attempt notification when configured
    Ntfy-->>Agent: Success or structured error result
  end
  Agent->>Agent: Graph returns to scheduler
  Agent->>Store: Compute fingerprint and persist verdict with results
  Store-->>Agent: Commit and return row ID
  Note over Agent,Store: Cycle completes. Scheduler waits before next cycle
  Note over Agent,Ntfy: Unhandled exception: log cycle failure and wait. Persistence is not guaranteed. No service remediation runs in this heartbeat.
